1
00:00:08,250 --> 00:00:09,833
Dear May Deer,

2
00:00:09,833 --> 00:00:11,667
With a lovely family,

3
00:00:11,667 --> 00:00:15,250
Dreaming of growing up each day.

4
00:00:15,250 --> 00:00:17,167
Shy Chuan-Chuan Pangolin,

5
00:00:17,167 --> 00:00:18,667
Quiet, with not a word to say,

6
00:00:18,667 --> 00:00:19,667
Curls up like a popcorn ball.

7
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:21,667
Curls up like a popcorn ball.

8
00:00:21,833 --> 00:00:22,333
Curls up like a popcorn ball.

9
00:00:22,333 --> 00:00:22,917
Don’t be shy!

10
00:00:23,083 --> 00:00:23,917
Don’t be shy!

11
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:24,500
Sing out loud!

12
00:00:24,667 --> 00:00:25,833
Sing out loud!

13
00:00:25,833 --> 00:00:27,167
Let your imagination shine!

14
00:00:30,417 --> 00:00:31,167
Good friends in the forest,

15
00:00:31,167 --> 00:00:33,083
Growing and playing together,

16
00:00:33,083 --> 00:00:34,000
Happy May Deer and Chuan-Chuan!

17
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,500
ODEER MAYO / Happy May Deer and Chuan-Chuan

18
00:00:37,676 --> 00:00:40,082
Afternoon Tea Time

19
00:00:43,583 --> 00:00:47,417
May invited her friends over to play this afternoon.

20
00:00:48,333 --> 00:00:50,667
Ding-dong! Ding-dong!

21
00:00:50,667 --> 00:00:54,500
My friends are almost here! I can’t wait! I’m so excited!

22
00:00:54,833 --> 00:00:56,583
Right, Little Deer?

23
00:00:56,583 --> 00:00:57,833
Little Deer!

24
00:00:58,583 --> 00:00:59,917
Oh, they’re here!

25
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:02,583
May!

26
00:01:02,833 --> 00:01:04,167
Chuan-Chuan! Jumi Rabbit!

27
00:01:04,167 --> 00:01:05,333
Welcome!

28
00:01:05,667 --> 00:01:08,000
May, thanks for inviting us over.

29
00:01:09,667 --> 00:01:10,083
Come on in!

30
00:01:12,083 --> 00:01:17,083
These are my radishes: Little Radish, Chubby Radish, and Big Radish.

31
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:20,500
And these are my big, medium, and tiny leaves.

32
00:01:23,250 --> 00:01:24,917
Mom, our guests are here!

33
00:01:25,167 --> 00:01:25,917
Hello, ma’am!

34
00:01:25,917 --> 00:01:29,500
Welcome, kids! I’ve prepared some yummy snacks for you.

35
00:01:29,833 --> 00:01:31,750
Wow! What are they?

36
00:01:32,083 --> 00:01:35,500
This is Mama Deer’s special Ruby Afternoon Tea.

37
00:01:35,583 --> 00:01:39,917
There’s tasty carrot juice, cherry tomatoes, and papaya jelly.

38
00:01:40,167 --> 00:01:42,250
They’re full of nutrients. Dig in!

39
00:01:42,667 --> 00:01:44,833
Thank you, Auntie!

40
00:01:44,833 --> 00:01:47,417
Mm-hmm.

41
00:01:48,167 --> 00:01:50,583
May, what’s wrong?

42
00:01:50,833 --> 00:01:53,000
I don’t like carrots.

43
00:01:53,250 --> 00:01:56,167
Because I think carrots smell

44
00:01:56,333 --> 00:01:59,000
like eating a moldy old log.

45
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:08,750
But Mom knows I don’t like them and still tells me to eat them every time.

46
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:11,833
Little Deer

47
00:02:13,417 --> 00:02:14,750
Really?

48
00:02:14,833 --> 00:02:15,833
My mommy says

49
00:02:15,833 --> 00:02:18,250
carrots are like beautiful red rubies.

50
00:02:18,250 --> 00:02:21,000
They make your eyes beautiful!

51
00:02:21,750 --> 00:02:25,833
Look! Don’t my eyes sparkle?

52
00:02:25,833 --> 00:02:26,417
Mwah!

53
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:30,333
Your eyes really are sparkling!

54
00:02:30,583 --> 00:02:34,083
But I don’t like Mr. Tomato.

55
00:02:34,083 --> 00:02:36,667
I think it tastes like…

56
00:02:37,083 --> 00:02:39,583
a slimy slug!

57
00:02:44,667 --> 00:02:47,083
Hahaha! How could that be?

58
00:02:47,250 --> 00:02:50,250
I think tomatoes are little suns shining in the universe.

59
00:02:50,333 --> 00:02:52,833
They give me lots of energy!

60
00:02:52,833 --> 00:02:54,250
Nom!

61
00:02:54,250 --> 00:02:57,167
What do you think, Chuan-Chuan?

62
00:02:58,167 --> 00:02:58,917
Uh…

63
00:02:58,917 --> 00:03:01,583
I like both carrots and tomatoes.

64
00:03:01,583 --> 00:03:02,333
But…

65
00:03:02,583 --> 00:03:04,750
I hate papaya.

66
00:03:04,750 --> 00:03:08,833
It’s slippery and mushy, and tastes like spit.

67
00:03:09,417 --> 00:03:10,167
Mm-hmm.

68
00:03:10,167 --> 00:03:11,250
How can that be?

69
00:03:11,250 --> 00:03:14,167
Mom says papaya is like an orange jewel from a tree spirit.

70
00:03:14,167 --> 00:03:16,833
It keeps my tummy regular and gives me endless energy!

71
00:03:17,750 --> 00:03:18,917
Oh, I’ve got an idea!

72
00:03:18,917 --> 00:03:20,667
Let’s secretly trade our food.

73
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:25,167
We can eat what the other person likes, and then we’ll finish everything on our plates!

74
00:03:25,833 --> 00:03:28,583
Wow, you’re clever! Let’s trade!

75
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:38,583
All gone!

76
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:46,500
So even your favorite food gets yucky if you eat too much of it.

77
00:03:46,500 --> 00:03:50,000
Kids, there’s a delicious dessert feast coming up!

78
00:03:50,667 --> 00:03:52,500
Oh, no!

79
00:03:52,500 --> 00:03:55,250
We’re too full to eat another thing!

80
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:57,417
We can go play for a while

81
00:03:57,417 --> 00:03:59,083
and burn off some energy.

82
00:03:59,083 --> 00:04:01,750
Then we’ll get hungry and have room for dessert later!

83
00:04:04,583 --> 00:04:06,833
Heave-ho! Heave-ho! Heave-ho!

84
00:04:06,833 --> 00:04:09,083
The children happily went off to play together.

85
00:04:10,833 --> 00:04:13,083
Let’s play a make-believe game with these blocks!

86
00:04:13,417 --> 00:04:16,250
I’ll use my imagination to defeat the foods I don’t like!

87
00:04:16,583 --> 00:04:19,583
Look! This block is a Carrot Superhero Candy!

88
00:04:19,750 --> 00:04:21,000
I’ll gobble it up in one bite!

89
00:04:21,583 --> 00:04:22,583
Nom!

90
00:04:23,333 --> 00:04:25,667
Now I have a superhero’s night vision!

91
00:04:26,167 --> 00:04:26,417
Hah!

92
00:04:27,833 --> 00:04:29,167
Wow, that’s amazing!

93
00:04:29,333 --> 00:04:32,167
Okay, this one is a Tomato Popping Candy!

94
00:04:32,250 --> 00:04:33,333
Nom!

95
00:04:33,333 --> 00:04:36,500
I ate it, and now I’m a bouncing champion!

96
00:04:36,667 --> 00:04:37,583
Mwah!

97
00:04:38,500 --> 00:04:41,500
And this is Papaya Invisibility Candy!

98
00:04:41,667 --> 00:04:42,250
Nom!

99
00:04:44,917 --> 00:04:45,667
I-I’m invisible!

100
00:04:57,667 --> 00:04:59,667
Kids, dessert is ready!

101
00:05:07,583 --> 00:05:10,083
It’s filled with all kinds of delicious ingredients.

102
00:05:12,250 --> 00:05:14,833
That block game was so much fun!

103
00:05:15,750 --> 00:05:18,417
Yeah! I got superhero night vision!

104
00:05:19,750 --> 00:05:22,000
B-being invisible was fun, too!

105
00:05:22,333 --> 00:05:23,917
Vroom, vroom, vroom, vroom!

106
00:05:24,417 --> 00:05:26,750
Haha, this cake is delicious!

107
00:05:26,750 --> 00:05:29,417
It’s so good! I want another slice. Mwah!

108
00:05:30,250 --> 00:05:33,833
I’m glad everyone likes the Ruby Cake so much.

109
00:05:33,833 --> 00:05:37,917
It’s packed with nutritious carrots, papaya, and cherry tomatoes.

110
00:05:38,417 --> 00:05:39,583
Huh?

111
00:05:39,750 --> 00:05:41,250
Oh…

112
00:05:41,417 --> 00:05:44,583
I didn’t expect tomatoes to taste good when I’m hungry!

113
00:05:44,583 --> 00:05:48,000
Yeah! Papaya doesn’t taste like spit anymore, either.

114
00:05:48,167 --> 00:05:51,583
I think food tastes extra good when you share it with good friends.

115
00:05:51,583 --> 00:05:55,083
Let’s eat together, together, together!

116
00:05:57,083 --> 00:05:58,083
Hahahaha!

117
00:05:59,167 --> 00:06:02,167
Sharing anything with you is the most fun!
